\details{
Low-dimensional simulators such as \code{\link[=JM_sim_ISCP]{JM_sim_ISCP()}} return \code{list(X, S)}.
\code{X} contains longitudinal rows with subject id \code{i}, visit time \code{tim}, and
biomarker value \code{y}; \code{S} contains one survival row per subject with \code{i},
observed time \code{Ti}, and event indicator \code{del}.

The high-dimensional simulator \code{\link[=drawY100]{drawY100()}} returns \code{list(X, S, y)}. \code{X}
and \code{S} use the same longitudinal/survival contract, while \code{y} is a matrix
whose columns are candidate biomarkers aligned to the rows of \code{X}.
